    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Adding a number and its reverse gives another useful pattern.\n\n(10x+y)+(10y+x)=11x+11y=11(x+y)",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So if the digit sum is 10, the number plus its reverse is 110—no matter whether the number is 19, 28, 37, 46 or 64.\n\nThis identity is about the sum of digits, not their order.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
