    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The chapter often says a number is a multiple of its digit sum.\n\nSuppose the units digit is 2 more than the tens digit. Let tens=x, units=x+2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Number = 10x+(x+2)=11x+2\nDigit sum = 2x+2\n\nIf the number is 4 times its digit sum:\n11x+2 = 4(2x+2)\n3x=6\nx=2\n\nThe number is 24. Check: 2+4=6 and 4×6=24.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
